                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I am going back and forth on this game. Honestly if it weren't for the art, it would be much easier to make up my mind.\nAs it stands, I would give it 7/10, only because despite the art I genuinely enjoyed the game.\n\nPros:\nLots of content  would take a lot of time to play through and get all of the different endings.\nThe main character is relatable, and all of the datable characters are likeable. \nStory is fluffy and cute, believable well written dialogue for the most part.\nBuy all the clothes. \nMake all the pancakes. \n\nCons:\ndat chin tho...\nJokes aside, my biggest complaint with the game is the art. Although I will say after a few hours of playing my irritation with the art subsided to a degree, but thats not to say that it grew on me because even after a few hours of play I would find myself distracted by the seemingly disjointed chins of literally every single character in the game. If you don't think you can get past the art, don't bother with this game. Even the CG's are pretty wonky looking.\nSome might not like the stat raising aspect (though I personally don't mind it)\nThe story lacks any real depth, (again, I didn't necessarily mind this myself. For what it is, I think this is just fine, though others might be disappointed with this.)\n\n",
